The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ctx = blk_mq_get_ctx(q);
hctx = blk_mq_map_queue(q, ctx->cpu);
data->hctx = hctx;
```
Reason:
When the system runs out of requests and goes to sleep, the context (`ctx`) and hardware context (`hctx`) are not updated in the `map ctx` structure. If the request (`rq->mq_ctx`) points to this outdated context, it can lead to incorrect locking when inserting new requests, potentially corrupting the request list (`ctx->rq_list`).

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
data->hctx = alloc_data.hctx;
data->ctx = alloc_data.ctx;
data->hctx->queued++;
```
Reason:
These statements ensure that the `hctx` and `ctx` in the `map ctx` structure are updated with the current values from `alloc_data`, which reflects the correct context after the allocation. This prevents the request from pointing to an outdated context, thus avoiding the risk of corrupting the request list when new requests are inserted.

